WEBVTT

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:23.840
<b>We're about to open!</b>

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:23.840
Today's specials: "Potatoes in Oden"

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya Nobu

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Potatoes in Oden</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:01:10.050
What is the must-try item the palace guards 
of the parallel universe encountered?!

00:00:33.010 --> 00:10:28.040
<b>Episode 1 "Potatoes in Oden"</b>

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.520
<b>Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:49.660
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:49.660
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.760
Tired, huh, Hans?

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.620
Running all the way to the 
forest in heavy gear.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.660
The new company commander 
isn't messing around!

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.430
Well then, how about a nightcap?

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.800
Found a pretty good pub recently.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.670
Really?

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.270
That good?

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.800
Besides, today your coffers are full.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.170
I mean today is...

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.110
...Payday!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.880
Both of the moons are out.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.410
We don't need a light to show our way.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.050
Look. It's that place, over there.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:13.550
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.550
This sign, what does it say?

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.090
Apparently it says "Izakaya Nobu."

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.690
Izakaya Nobu?

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.530
Yup. It's the owner's name.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.930
Nobu Taishou.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.960
Call him Taishou (Chief) in there.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.200
Huh.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.800
So what do they serve here?

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.940
You'll find out once you're 
eating. And you'll like it.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.170
If you say so.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:36.440
The canteen's serving kartoffel 
every single day.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.340
Wouldn't mind something el—

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:38.880
Hey!

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.410
Is this really okay?

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.710
What do you mean?

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.080
Can we pay?

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.520
That's glass!

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.990
That reminds me, doesn't your 
father work with glass?

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.420
Yes. Glass is a luxury.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.520
Don't worry.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.960
This place even lets you carry a tab.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.460
In we go!

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.630
Welcome!

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.500
Welcome.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.700
I'm back, Shinobu-chan.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.770
A party of two, is it?

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.240
Please take a seat.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.540
I'll have a whatsontap.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.780
He'll have the same.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.880
That'll be two draft beers.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.350
Hang on, what was that 'whatsonsomething.'

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.460
Ah, whatsontap?

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.760
Just sit tight and drink it.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.090
You'll be surprised.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:28.930
Drink it?

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:29.930
Is it alcohol?

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.500
It's ale.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.070
You can bitch about the company 
commander after you had some.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.800
Here you go, two draft beers.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.000
Excuse my reach.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.740
<i>This is glass, too?!</i>

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.540
<i>And just look at this ale.</i>

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.940
<i>No, this whatsontap's translucent 
amber-gold color and its fine bubbles...</i>

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.350
<i>My hand is being sucked in.</i>

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.720
Brr!

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.850
It shocked me too at first!

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.920
All right, let's get to it and drink.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.360
O-Oh.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.990
Prosit!

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.160
Enjoy.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.860
Enjoy.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.200
Thank you.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.260
<b>Gulp</b>

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.340
That is good!

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.240
Come on, drink.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.170
No matter how much you chill ale, it's...

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.310
Just come on and drink it.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:20.550
<b>Fizz</b>

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.580
<b>Fizz</b>

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:21.910
<b>Fizz</b>

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.600
So, Hans?

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.760
Good, huh?

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.730
I feel cleansed.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:46.300
I've never drank such 
clean tasting ale before!

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.470
Is it because it's cold?

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:49.710
Or because it's fresh?

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.280
Whatever it is, it's the 
best ale I've ever drunk!

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.780
Was it that good?

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.850
May I bring you another?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:56.850
Sure!

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.820
Another whatsontap!

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.580
All right.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.220
Thank you.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.220
Another draft beer!

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:02.890
<b>Pop</b>

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.690
So about that company commander.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.490
Hey.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:07.630
What is that?

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.990
It's a snack.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:14.030
<b>Boiled Edamame with Salt</b>

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:14.030
<b>The absolute classic beer snack!</b>

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.830
It's beans, boiled in salt water.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.000
They can't even be bothered 
to shell it for you?

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:20.100
No, this shell is infused with 
salt, so you eat it like this.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.540
<b>Pop</b>

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.240
Giving you the perfect salty punch!

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.350
It can't be that much different 
than salt-boiled torkan beans.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.390
Good, huh?

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:36.850
Nikolaus, this is bad.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.090
I can't stop!

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.060
Yeah.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.330
You can't, right?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.200
And this goes very well with whatsontap.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.060
No fair, what about me?

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.200
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.740
I've been waiting for you, whatsontap!

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:51.900
<b>Pop</b>

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.240
<b>Fizz</b>

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.710
So good!

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:57.610
I told you so.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.880
<i>Appetizer.</i>

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:58.680
<b>Pop</b>

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.040
<i>Whatsontap.</i>

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.040
<b>Fizz</b>

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.180
<i>Appetizer.</i>

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.050
<b>Pop</b>

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.250
<i>Whatsontap.</i>

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.250
<b>Fizz</b>

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.310
<i>Appeti—</i>

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:03.950
<b>Empty</b>

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.320
<i>That was close.</i>

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.690
<i>If these beans hadn't run out,</i>

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:12.020
<i>I would've spent the rest 
of my life to eating beans.</i>

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.630
<i>This restaurant is amazing.</i>

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.760
<i>Full of unfamiliar writing and food.</i>

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:20.300
<i>Are these people citizens 
of a faraway region?</i>

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:27.240
<i>She spreads her pure smile all around and 
works as diligently as a honey bee.</i>

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:29.840
<i>There is nobody as industrious as her!</i>

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.180
<i>And then this man at the counter.</i>

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.280
<i>Make no mistake, he has the aura 
of a great, historic hero.</i>

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.550
<i>This is no ordinary place!</i>

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.590
Taishou, what will you be feeding us today?

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:44.090
Today, it's oden.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.620
Odin?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.130
Here you go.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.630
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.360
It's hot, so please be careful.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.130
<i>A stew, huh?</i>

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.970
<i>How very welcome for this time of year.</i>

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:04.480
<b>Steaming daikon radish and a hot egg!
 It'll drive the chill out of all your bones!</b>

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:04.480
<b>Nobu's Specialty Oden</b>

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.800
<i>Oden.</i>

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.610
<i>The name reminds me of one of 
the northern peoples' gods.</i>

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:04.480
<i>Is this some kind of traditional 
dish from a cold land?</i>

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.780
This doesn't have any Wurst in it?

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:07.980
Wurst?

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.010
Oh, you mean wieners.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.480
Those are good, but
I didn't put any in today.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.990
I'll give you this instead.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:18.390
<i>What's this supposed to be?</i>

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.760
<i>Not to mention, I don't recognize 
most of these ingredients.</i>

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.730
<i>I can't begin to imagine 
what this tastes like.</i>

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.870
<i>This broth has a gentle smell though.</i>

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.970
<i>Here we go.</i>

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.600
Starting with the daikon, huh?

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:38.980
<i>He said "daikon," but what 
is that supposed to mean?</i>

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.730
<i>I don't get it... but...</i>

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.210
The flavor is all soaked in, right?

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.190
Delicious!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:54.130
<i>What an amazing warmth for your body, 
battered and chilled from the drills.</i>

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:49.850
<b>Sproing</b>

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:56.790
<i>It's relaxing the very core of my body.</i>

00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:02.730
This is none other than the food eaten 
by the northern gods themselves!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.010
Oh.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.910
Is this a kartoffel?

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:09.810
What's wrong?

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.340
You don't care for potatoes?

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.950
You call kartoffel "potatoes" 
in this establishment?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:18.220
Since I've been born, I've been 
eating them for over twenty years.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.120
Can't get excited about eating 
them now, after all this.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.190
Hmm.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.690
Why don't you try putting 
a little of this on them?

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.320
You put mustard on them?

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.790
It's not really mustard. It's karashi.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:29.930
Just try it.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:33.330
They use mustard to hide the stench of meat.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.330
<i>Putting that on won't do anything.</i>

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:45.710
<b>Sting</b>

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.880
<i>The spiciness pierces your sinuses.</i>

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.410
<i>This isn't mustard!</i>

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.450
<b>Warm</b>

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:50.780
<i>The broth is complex and rich and sweet,</i>

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.050
<b>Sting</b>

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.620
<b>Warm</b>

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.550
<i>and it works exquisitely 
with this spiciness!</i>

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.550
<b>Sting</b>

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:53.550
<b>Warm</b>

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:56.450
What is this? Is this really be a kartoffel?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.060
It's so fluffy and different!

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.560
See, the potatoes are good, huh?

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:05.160
I never knew the world had 
such delicious potatoes.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.630
Right, Niko...

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.970
What's that?

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:11.440
This is atsukan (hot sake).

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:12.640
It goes great with the oden.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:13.910
Taishou!

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.810
Me, too, please!

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:17.640
All right.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.310
One atsukan, please.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.250
Allow me to pour your first cup.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:26.420
Thank you.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.060
<i>What a fragrance!</i>

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:36.260
<i>Heating it up makes the 
alcohol's scent unfold!</i>

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.960
<i>This is unlike wine or mead.</i>

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.700
<i>And it's strong!</i>

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.540
<i>But it's not like schnapps.</i>

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.870
<i>It's a clear and calm kind of strength.</i>

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.810
<i>It warms your entire body from the core!</i>

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.250
That is so good!

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.780
If you keep drinking like that, you're 
going to get hebereke.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:01.750
<i>Hebe Eryuke...	The goddess pouring wine?</i>

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.150
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.120
<i>This must the wine of legends 
that the gods imbibed...</i>

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.760
<i>Is this nectar?!</i>

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.530
That's right, just like 
the ale and the beans.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.440
That's so good!

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.510
This is happiness.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.810
The joy of another land is 
traversing all through my body!

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:30.350
Oden and atsukan are amazing!

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:32.920
Here you go.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:38.520
Isn't charging a single silver tropfen 
for all of that rather too cheap?

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.120
It's fine.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:44.530
Seeing a guest's happy face is 
worth all the money in the world!

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:48.970
What's wrong, Hans?

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.470
B-Bye...

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.510
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.370
Thank you!

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:58.680
Aah, that was so good!

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:02.010
We never did get around to talking 
about the company commander though.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.250
Who cares about him?

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:05.150
Hey, listen to me!

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.650
You better not tell him 
about that place. Ever!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:09.190
Of course not!

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.020
Well?

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.760
I wasn't wrong, was I?

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:13.390
You were not.

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.230
I've never been this 
pleasantly drunk before.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.260
And...

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.700
Want me to finish what you're going to say?

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:23.840
Shut up!

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.340
Mind your own business!

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus!

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:39.450
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:40.120
Wow, the hot staple from any izakaya 
is undergoing a huge transformation!

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:45.890
Ryuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:46.460
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.060
That oden looked really good.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.160
I bet that it really is. I mean that daikon!

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.400
And that Kartoffel.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:58.140
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:58.140
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:55.630
When you put mustard on Kartoffel, well,

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:58.140
<b>[Kartoffel = German for potato]</b>

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.140
then you will go for 
whatsontap and hot sake.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.900
But you end up making too much.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:02.540
When you try to use stuff up, you 
end up with a ridiculous amount.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.540
<b>Oden uses a lot of ingredients, so you often end up making too much</b>

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.380
So, these ingredients for 
oden, daikon and potato.

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:08.780
I'm going to make them into 
a totally different snack.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.350
<b>Using the two oden ingredients, daikon and 
potato, to make a totally different snack!</b>

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:09.350
Wow!

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:14.350
<b>Oden potato salad
 [Ingredients (serves 2)]
 Oden potatoes - 2
 Onion - 1/4
 Fukujinzuke relish - to taste
 French dressing - 1 tablespoon
 Mayonnaise - 2 tablespoons
 Coarse black pepper - a pinch

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.920
Turning the oden potatoes 
into a potato salad.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.350
Turning the oden daikon into a steak.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.520
First, the onion. Slice it thinly.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:17.120
Got it.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.720
We want the texture to be light,

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:22.260
<b>Mash the potato while it's hot</b>

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:23.900
so cut the onion perpendicular to the 
fibers, then quickly rinse them.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:24.400
Got it.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:29.330
This membrane on the surface, 
that's where the bite is.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.330
I didn't know that.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:33.040
To keep it simple, this. French 
dressing to marinate the onions.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:33.910
That's easy, I like it.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:35.940
It's been about five minutes of marinating.

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.080
The potato.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.680
While it's hot, put it in 
the marinated onions.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.380
Then, mash it with a fork.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.680
<b>Reduce the moisture of the daikon and place 
it in the frying pan before turning the stove on</b>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.250
I see.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.320
While the potato is cooling, I'd like to 
prepare the other item, the daikon steak.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.120
Nice, that's so efficient.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.120
Lightly oil the pan.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:55.460
So the daikon sputters when 
there's too much broth in it.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.130
So let's wipe it off.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:01.530
Another point. If you put this daikon into a hot 
frying pan, the moisture will still explode out.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.100
So place them in there while 
the pan is still cool.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:05.440
Got it.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:08.910
The daikon looks really tasty when 
it has this nice grill mark.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:09.370
That's true!

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.240
When one side is done, flip it over,

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.880
place a lid on it, and cook on 
low heat for about 5 minutes.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.120
The potato has cooled down quite a bit.

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.590
Now we add the mayonnaise.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:25.790
Today, I'd like to add some things I have 
here to make it a bit more Japanese.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.060
Oh, what are you adding?

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.390
It's this.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.290
Oh, fukujinzuke?

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:34.200
That's right! It's sweet, crunchy, 
giving the dish this nice touch.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.070
And isn't the color pretty?

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.440
When it looks pretty, it's 
a bit more exciting, right?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.440
Definitely.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:41.710
Lastly, the sauce.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:42.310
Okay.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:48.750
<b>Making the sauce
 Combine in frying pan
 Sake (2 teaspoons)  mirin (1 teaspoon)  soy sauce (2 teaspoons)</b>

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.980
What are you going for?

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:48.450
Sake, mirin, soy sauce... 
a standard Japanese sauce?

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:51.920
The bubbles are getting small and popping.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.990
This is when we add the 
last ingredient, butter.

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.490
What? Butter?

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:55.990
We're giving it more body.

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:58.960
Now make sure to combine the butter 
well with the other ingredients.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.790
Oh gosh, I can't handle this 
butter-soy sauce scent. It's too enticing!

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.400
Then you get this kind of rich consistency.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:08.130
That's nice, the grill marks and this sauce.

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:10.070
You know, when you're having alcohol,

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:17.710
<b>Oden potato salad and oden daikon steak</b>

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:13.240
you want to have a bite or two 
of many different things.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:17.710
That's when oden can be transformed 
into different flavors.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:21.250
I think this is great when you're 
drinking, so please try making these.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.750
Couldn't have said it better! 
These are irresistible.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.850
The potato from the oden 
turns into potato salad,

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:27.650
the broth-laden daikon turns into a steak.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:30.190
Both really easy but so delicious!

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:32.660
Everybody, please try 
this at home! Thank you!

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:57.980
<b>Next Time...
Juicy Karaage</b>

